.TH start-cli-package-host-binding-set-address-enabled 1  "set-address-enabled "
.SH NAME
start\-cli\-package\-host\-binding\-set\-address\-enabled \- Set a gateway address enabled for a binding
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-cli package host binding set\-address\-enabled\fR <\fB\-\-address\fR> [\fB\-\-enabled\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-insecure\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINTERNAL_PORT\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set a gateway address enabled for a binding
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-address\fR \fI<ADDRESS>\fR
One of the binding\*(Aqs addresses (IP, <name>.local or domain), with :port when it serves several ports; a JSON HostnameInfo also works
.TP
\fB\-\-enabled\fR \fI<ENABLED>\fR
Enable or disable this binding
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-insecure\fR
Accept plaintext traffic that devices on this network, or private networks routed to it over IPv4, can read and alter, including passwords
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIINTERNAL_PORT\fR>
Internal port number
